.TH LLAPI_IO_SCOPE_SET 3 2026-09-30 "Lustre User API" "Lustre Library Functions"
.SH NAME
llapi_io_scope_set, llapi_io_scope_clear \- restrict I/O on a file descriptor to a layout subset
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <lustre/lustreapi.h>
.PP
.BI "int llapi_io_scope_set(int " fd ", const struct ll_ioc_io_scope *" scope );
.PP
.BI "int llapi_io_scope_clear(int " fd );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR llapi_io_scope_set()
stores
.I scope
on the open file descriptor
.IR fd .
Later
.BR read (2),
.BR write (2),
.BR lseek (2),
.BR ftruncate (2),
and
.BR fallocate (2)
calls on
.I fd
are limited to that subset of the file layout.
.PP
.BR llapi_io_scope_clear()
restores whole-file I/O by setting a zeroed
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_FILE
scope.
.PP
.I scope
is an
.B ll_ioc_io_scope
structure:
.PP
.nf
struct ll_ioc_io_scope {
        __u32           ios_scope;           /* enum ll_io_scope */
        __u32           ios_flags;           /* reserved; must be 0 */
        __u32           ios_mirror_id;       /* MIRROR; STRIPE */
        __u32           ios_comp_id;         /* OBJECT: comp; else 0 */
        __u32           ios_stripe_idx;      /* STRIPE: rel; OBJECT: abs */
        __u32           ios_layout_version;  /* 0 = use fd layout version */
        struct lu_fid   ios_obj_fid;         /* OBJECT: object FID; else 0 */
        __u64           ios_padding[2];      /* must be 0 */
};
.fi
.PP
.I ios_scope
selects the subset:
.TP
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_FILE
The whole file, addressed by file offset.
.I O_DIRECT
is not required.
.I ios_mirror_id
and
.I ios_layout_version
must be 0.
.TP
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_MIRROR
The single FLR mirror
.IR ios_mirror_id ,
addressed by file offset.
.I ios_mirror_id
must be in the range 1 to
.BR MIRROR_ID_MAX .
The scope is intended for
.B O_DIRECT
I/O, and is only accepted on a descriptor opened with
.BR O_DIRECT .
The mirror is not looked up when the scope is set.
If an FLR file has no mirror
.IR ios_mirror_id ,
later I/O on
.I fd
fails with
.I errno
set to
.BR EINVAL .
On a non-FLR file
.I ios_mirror_id
is ignored and later I/O addresses the whole file.
.TP
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_STRIPE
Reserved.
One object, addressed by file offset.
.I ios_mirror_id
selects the mirror, and the component is the one in that mirror covering
the offset.
.I ios_stripe_idx
selects among the objects of that component backing the offset
(for example data or which parity); 0 is the first one.
.I ios_comp_id
must be 0.
.TP
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_OBJECT
Reserved.
One object, addressed by object offset, located by
.RI ( ios_comp_id ", " ios_stripe_idx ),
by
.IR ios_obj_fid ,
or by both, which must then name the same object.
.I ios_stripe_idx
is the absolute stripe index within
.IR ios_comp_id .
.I ios_comp_id
0 means the pair is absent, and
.I ios_stripe_idx
must then be 0.
.I ios_mirror_id
must be 0.
.PP
For
.BR LL_IO_SCOPE_MIRROR ,
.I ios_layout_version
0 uses the layout version recorded on
.I fd
by the last resync lease; if there is none, no check is made.
A non-zero value replaces that version.
Currently only
.BR write (2),
.BR ftruncate (2),
and
.BR fallocate (2)
on an FLR file compare it with the current layout generation and fail with
.I errno
set to
.B ESTALE
on a mismatch.
.BR read (2)
and
.BR lseek (2)
do not check it.
On a non-FLR file it is ignored and not sent to the OSTs.
.PP
The reserved scopes are rejected with
.BR -EOPNOTSUPP .
Any other value of
.I ios_scope
is rejected with
.BR -EINVAL .
.PP
Fields that are not used by the selected scope must be zero, so that they
stay available for the reserved scopes.
For
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_FILE
and
.BR LL_IO_SCOPE_MIRROR
this means
.IR ios_comp_id ,
.IR ios_stripe_idx ,
and
.IR ios_obj_fid
(including
.IR f_seq ,
.IR f_oid ,
and
.IR f_ver ).
.I ios_flags
and
.I ios_padding
must be 0 for every scope.
.PP
The scope is stored per open file description and is shared with the
.B LL_IOC_FLR_SET_MIRROR
ioctl:
setting a mirror ID with that ioctl is equivalent to setting a
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_MIRROR
scope, and setting mirror ID 0 is equivalent to
.BR llapi_io_scope_clear() .
.SH RETURN VALUES
.B llapi_io_scope_set()
and
.B llapi_io_scope_clear()
return 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 15
.B -EBADF
.I fd
is not a valid file descriptor.
.TP
.B -EFAULT
.I scope
points to memory that could not be read.
.TP
.B -EINVAL
.I scope
is NULL,
.I ios_scope
is not a known value,
a field that must be zero is not,
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_MIRROR
was requested with
.I ios_mirror_id
0 or greater than
.BR MIRROR_ID_MAX ,
or a scope other than
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_FILE
was set on a descriptor that is not
.BR O_DIRECT .
.TP
.B -ENOTTY
.I fd
does not refer to a Lustre file.
.TP
.B -EOPNOTSUPP
.I ios_scope
is
.B LL_IO_SCOPE_STRIPE
or
.BR LL_IO_SCOPE_OBJECT .
.SH EXAMPLES
Read from mirror 1. The descriptor must be opened with
.BR O_DIRECT :
.EX
        struct ll_ioc_io_scope scope = { 0 };
        void *buf = NULL;
        int fd, rc;
\&
        fd = open(path, O_RDONLY | O_DIRECT);
        if (fd < 0)
                return -errno;
\&
        scope.ios_scope = LL_IO_SCOPE_MIRROR;
        scope.ios_mirror_id = 1;
        rc = llapi_io_scope_set(fd, &scope);
        if (rc < 0)
                goto out;
\&
        /* O_DIRECT requires an aligned buffer. */
        rc = -posix_memalign(&buf, 4096, 4096);
        if (rc < 0)
                goto out;
        if (read(fd, buf, 4096) < 0)
                rc = -errno;
\&
        llapi_io_scope_clear(fd);
out:
        free(buf);
        close(fd);
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B llapi_io_scope_set()
and
.B llapi_io_scope_clear()
are part of the
.BR lustre (7)
user application interface library since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_59-4-g6dac0dd45f
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (2),
.BR lustreapi (7)
